{
  "description": "External conservation and repair works to the Grade II listed dwelling at 19 Village Way, comprising repointing of defective masonry joints in lime mortar, with tuck pointing to the front elevation and flush pointing to affected areas of the side and rear elevations; cleaning and repointing of the entrance steps; installation of Helifix/Helibar crack-stitch repairs; and like-for-like replacement of up to 100 damaged bricks.\r\rRepairs to the roof and parapet comprising repointing of defective coping-stone joints; reinstatement of missing coping clamps; localised repair of coping stones, with like-for-like replacement where beyond repair; and reinstatement of missing mortar flaunching to the roof and parapet.\r\rRepair of five timber window hoods to the front elevation and repair of existing timber windows where practicable, together with like-for-like replacement of two lower box-casement windows in timber to match the existing profiles, glazing pattern, detailing and finish.\r\rLike-for-like repair of a defective section of the rear downpipe, together with preparation and redecoration of existing windows, doors, cast iron and other painted external surfaces to match the existing colour and finish.\r\rAnalysis of existing mortar samples to inform the specification of compatible lime mortar matching the original composition, colour, aggregate, texture, joint profile and finish, with retention of all sound historic fabric.\r",
